1
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Most motorcycles run on petrol, this one runs on blood!

2
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:34,000
I Bought a Vampire Motorcycle is a comedy, horror
film directed by Dirk Campbell.

3
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
When a motorbike gang kills an occultist, the evil spirit
he was summoning inhabits a damaged bike.

4
00:26:56,000 --> 00:27:02,000
The bike is then bought and restored, but reveals its true nature when it tries to
exact vengance on the gang, and anyone else who gets in its way.

5
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Noddy, played by Neil Morrissey.

6
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Kim, played by Amanda Noar.

7
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:14,000
Inspector Cleaver, played by Michael Elphick.

8
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:58,000
Priest, played by Anthony Daniels.

9
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
Roach, played by Andrew Powell.

10
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
Chopper, played by George Rossi.

11
01:14:04,000 --> 01:14:10,000
I Bought a Vampire Motorcycle is a 1990 British comedy horror film about a motorcycle possessed by an evil
spirit, which rides by itself and kills people, particularly members of a particular motorcycle gang.

12
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
It stars Neil Morrissey as the bike's owner, Michael Elphick as a police inspector, and
Anthony Daniels as a priest who attempts to exorcise the bike's evil spirit.

13
01:27:32,000 --> 01:27:38,000
The film explores themes of supernatural, motorcycle, vampirism, birmingham.

14
01:34:16,000 --> 01:34:22,000
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
